---
servings: 4
---

Place @chicken thighs{500%g}(cut into chunks) into #slow cooker{}.

Add @shallots{2}(sliced), @green pepper{1}(roughly chopped), @baby corn{6}(cut in half), @sugar snap peas{50%g}(cut in half), @coriander{1%bunch}(finely chopped), @lemongrass{1%stick}, @lime leaves{5}, @sugar{3/2%tsp}, @soy sauce{4%tbsp} and @pepper{} into #slow cooker{}.
Sprinkle @flour{30%g} and stir thoroughly until everything is evenly mixed.

In a #pan{}, fry @Thai green curry paste{2%tbsp} until it loosens and becomes highly fragrant.
Pour in @coconut milk{400%ml} and combine together until cream has completely melted and sauce looks silky.

Pour sauce into the slow cooker, squeeze over the @lime{1/2}(juiced) and stir through well.
Replace the lid and cook on high for ~{3%hours}.

Cook @rice{2%cup} according to packet.
